@* One loading vocabulary (D-114): geometry-identical to index.html's boot indicator —
   same 48px ring, same stroke, same 20vh anchor — so a refresh reads as one ring that
   fills (real download progress) during runtime boot, then spins here, in place, while
   the page's data loads. The fetch has no progress signal (one atomic response), so this
   half is indeterminate by design; a determinate 25→100 walk was considered and rejected
   as a fabricated number. *@
<div class="loading-ring" aria-busy="true">
    <svg><circle class="track" r="40%" cx="50%" cy="50%" /><circle class="arc" r="40%" cx="50%" cy="50%" /></svg>
    <span class="cap">Loading…</span>
</div>
